ruby grimm eclipse is a bad license  video game not because it's a bad game  although it certainly is but because it  doesn't take any of the positive  qualities of the show it's based on sure  it looks like the show features the same  music and voice actors makes the  occasional callback but it lacks any of  its clever writing charm and personality  if there's one thing I expected this  game to get right it would have been  those things because of Ruby Grimm  Eclipse is a very unique example because  it was created in-house at roosterteeth  the same company responsible for the  show so rarely does a show have such  direct access to the talent behind the  show which based on and even with all  that advantage the game barely makes an  effort from a clip starts off with a  pretty solid premise by being a  four-player hack and slash action game  the style of gameplay lends itself well  to letting players mimic move fast and  stylish combat that's core to the show  but the game likes the budget  productions to be the Bayonetta like  that it needs to be sword instead ghost  with a simpler approach invoking dynasty  warriors instead which is perfectly  alright as long as the game still fun to  play it's fine it's not though each  chapter has you run through a linear  level fighting enemies with the  occasional dialogue and that's kind of  AIT's the environments while  nice-looking are large and empty you run  through these massive areas simply to  get to the next group of enemies to  fight and the time in between fights is  dull and boring and that's really all  you do is stop to fight enemies and then  move on sometimes it'll mix things up by  introducing a wave of enemies and then  another wave of enemies oh and what's  that over there  it's another wave of enemies sometimes  waves happen while you must defend an  objective however this objective takes  so little damage it might as well not  even be there it's not until halfway  through that something finally new  happens with this car escort mission but  it's not very fun and I rather go back  to the waves there's simply not enough  variety to the missions that by the end  of the second level you feel like you've  seen everything the game has to offer  because you kind of have the combat  itself isn't great either there isn't  really much in the way of combos so you  just kind of have to run up and spam the  buttons and hope you  except even that doesn't really work  enemies have this amazing ability to  block all your attacks which isn't  telegraphed well enough in the chaos in  battle so you'll be wailing on them for  a few seconds before you realize you  aren't actually doing any damage and  some of the systems feel like they're  really clashing against each other  rather than working together take these  enemies that you encounter around  halfway through they explode after  hitting them so the idea is you want to  hit them then dodge away or shoot them  from a distance but the game also says  hey you can counter these guys so you do  it because there's a button prompt and  the game says so and why not is the  game's telling you to do it  however this moves you right on top of  them guaranteeing that you'll be hit by  their explosion so your reward for using  the counter system is taking damage the  game also lacks any real tutorial which  at first seems fine since everything is  so basic you can pick up on the  mechanics just from playing at least  that's what I thought until I encounter  this ability on the skill tree which  describes a cool move your character can  do but doesn't tell you how to pull it  off after going through most of the game  not understanding how to activate the  skill I finally found it by looking up a  user made steam guide outside of the  game I'll repeat that a user guide not  found in the game turns out this whole  thing is related to team attacks to do a  team attack you must get an enemy in a  state where they can be attacked by your  teammates which is symbolized by this  silver icon above their head how do you  get them in the state it's completely  random once they're in this state  another teammate will see the icon in  bronze and then can run up and hit the  right bumper and do that special move  completing a team attack again none of  this is explained in the game at all as  I mentioned earlier it's the ties to the  show that really make this disappointing  the narrative holding these chapters  together is paper-thin  a small dialogue telling you where you  are and what your objective is but none  of it is particularly interesting the  first half has you running through an  uninspired retread of locations from the  show which is cool to see but offers  nothing new with them while the second  half does offer brand new places and  enemies they aren't particularly  interesting the attempts to develop a  more concrete narrative with brand new  characters comes in very late and falls  completely flat because it lacks any of  the punch from the original show and  dialogue delivery that is shockingly  poor  No how could I be so stupid initiating  the upload you did it  now can you proxy decision closes your  school prepare to meet your doom some of  the characters personalities do slip  through with the occasional line but  these moments are few and far between  the campaign ran me about three hours  and considering it stopped being fun  after the second level probably a good  thing the game does encourage you to  play again this time with a different  character but even if that was something  I wanted to do which it's not the  characters simply don't feel different  enough from each other to feel like I'm  getting a different experience if I  sound like I'm being overly harsh it's  because honestly I had pretty decent  expectations for this I'm a fan of the  show I think it would make a great video  game and there's a lot of potential  there this game squanders all of that  it's hard for me to even recommend the  most die-hard of Ruby fans who would be  okay with a somewhat mediocre game but  they get to hear some funny dialogue  considering the game's incredibly steep  $25 price points that's really who this  is for fans of the show and I think it's  such a missed opportunity that they  couldn't even capitalize on that  considering they had such direct access  to the creator's themselves hey  everybody thanks for watching this video  if you have been playing the game or  you're a fan of the show please let me  know in the comments below start a  conversation I enjoy having those with  people if you want to see more stuff  like this I hit that subscribe button it  really helps sound tells us that people  like this stuff and hey have a good day  better and better better and better  better and better better and better  better yeah oh yeah oh yeah better and  better better and better  booyah booyah booyah booyah booyah  booyah booyah booyah booyah booyah  booyah
 

